# Conventional Commits

Commit messages and pull request titles use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <description>
```

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.
- Description is imperative, lowercase, and has no trailing period.
- A scope is optional and names the area, for example `feat(pen): stop on the last letter`.
- The pull request title is the same single line. The body can explain the change; it does not repeat the title as a sentence.
